<section class="section flow">
  <h2>About the Society</h2>

  <p>The Wiveliscombe Civic and Historical Society is a community venture established in 1997.</p>

  <h3>Key Activities &amp; Aims</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Community Information:</strong> Informing the local community on issues that directly affect them.</li>
    <li><strong>Planning Scrutiny:</strong> Scrutinizing significant local planning applications.</li>
    <li><strong>Talks Programme:</strong> Presenting a programme of talks on subjects of general and community interest.</li>
    <li><strong>Local Collaboration:</strong> Working closely with other community organisations in Wiveliscombe for mutual benefit.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Organisation &amp; Funding</h3>
  <p>As a volunteer-run organisation, the society relies on income generated from membership fees, donations, and admission charges for talks.</p>

  <p>For further information about the Civic Society and our talks, please contact <strong>Pauline Homeshaw</strong> on <a href="tel:01984624564">01984 624564</a> or at <a href="mailto:homeshaw@btopenworld.com">homeshaw@btopenworld.com</a>.</p>
</section>

